{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm investigating why the MLE Rounds phase in the GPU prover takes LONGER at APC 300 (174ms) than at APC 0 (114ms) despite APC 300 having far fewer cells. The issue seems to be per-AIR overhead with 623 AIR instances at APC 300 vs 99 at APC 0.\n\nI need to understand the MLE rounds code path in the GPU prover:\n1. The main MLE round loop — where it iterates over AIRs or traces\n2. What per-AIR or per-trace work happens in each round\n3. The batched kernels that were already implemented (zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel, logup_batch_mle_kernel, batched_nondegen_mle_round_kernel)\n4. What CPU-side work remains per-AIR/per-trace between kernel launches\n5. Any sequential operations that can't be batched\n\nSearch in:\n- `crates/cuda-backend/src/` — look for files related to MLE, sumcheck, logup_zerocheck_mle\n- `crates/cuda-backend/cuda/src/` — the CUDA kernels\n\nI need file paths, line numbers, and the full loop structure to understand what creates per-AIR overhead in MLE rounds. Report the call chain from the MLE round entry point through all sub-operations."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016SBVHkQkrDLgfDXTKW2X5T","session_id":"f93534bb-5de3-4083-9e85-ad533ac466ab","uuid":"4897f73d-286a-4da4-9ca9-b3c44299832c","timestamp":"2026-04-14T04:03:54.571Z"}
