{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0176knSXpLjVFPnwrNKNfpcR","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I now have comprehensive information. Let me create a detailed summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary: Round 0 Per-AIR Processing Overhead Analysis\n\nBased on my investigation of `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/`, here's the complete breakdown of Round 0 processing:\n\n### **Multi-Stream Threshold & Dispatch** (lines 1066-1151)\n- **Threshold**: `>= 100 AIRs` triggers multi-streaming (line 1066)\n- **Max threads**: 8 (`NUM_ROUND0_STREAMS` at line 99)\n- **Round-robin assignment**: Height-sorted AIRs distributed round-robin across threads (lines 1140-1151) so each thread gets a balanced mix of large and small AIRs\n- **Barrier sync**: `current_stream_sync()` at line 1060 ensures prior GPU work visible to worker threads\n- **Rationale** (lines 1063-1065): With few large AIRs (APC 0 has ~20), each kernel saturates GPU and multi-threading adds memory pool overhead\n\n### **Per-Thread Pre-allocation** (lines 1038-1131)\n- **Percentile-based sizing** (95th percentile): Avoids enormous buffers from outlier AIRs\n- **Four buffers pre-allocated per thread**:\n  - `zc_intermediates`: Zerocheck DAG intermediate nodes\n  - `zc_temp_sums`: Zerocheck temp block sums\n  - `logup_intermediates`: Logup DAG intermediate nodes  \n  - `logup_temp_sums`: Logup fractional temp block sums\n- **Memory check**: Reduces `num_threads` if `num_threads * per_thread_bytes > 2GB` (line 1077)\n\n### **Per-AIR Work in `process_air_round0()`** (lines 152-322)\n\n**WorkItem struct** (lines 126-150) holds:\n- `single_pk`: Proving key pointer\n- `selectors_cube`, `public_values`, `eq_3bs`: Trace data pointers\n- `cached_mains`, `common_main`: Trace matrices\n- `eq_xis`: EQ evaluation tree (per n_lift)\n- `d_lambda_pows`, `beta_pows`: Challenge arrays\n- Pre-computed buffer capacities for all 4 buffers\n\n**Execution steps** (per AIR, per thread):\n\n1. **CPU setup** (lines 156-212):\n   - Extract constraint degree & parameters from pk\n   - Compute omega_root for coset domain (line 166)\n   - Collect main trace pointers into vector (lines 170-174)\n   - Upload main_parts to GPU (`to_device()` at line 175) — **PER-AIR GPU MALLOC**\n   - Check pre-allocated zerocheck buffer validity (lines 182-195)\n   - Call `evaluate_round0_constraints_gpu()` (lines 197-212) — **GPU KERNEL LAUNCH #1**\n\n2. **Zerocheck polynomial construction** (lines 214-242):\n   - **D2H copy**: `sum_buffer.to_host_on_current_stream()` (line 215) — **PER-AIR SYNC POINT**\n   - Transpose GPU evaluations (lines 217-222)\n   - `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` (lines 223-227) — **CPU iDFT #1** (~1-2ms per AIR)\n   - Coefficient extraction & normalization (lines 229-238)\n\n3. **Logup interactions evaluation** (lines 244-279):\n   - Build interaction DAG rules from symbolic constraints (NOT pre-allocated per AIR)\n   - Check pre-allocated logup buffers (lines 247-260)\n   - Call `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu()` (lines 262-279) — **GPU KERNEL LAUNCH #2**\n\n4. **Logup polynomial construction** (lines 281-314):\n   - **D2H copy**: `sum.to_host_on_current_stream()` (line 282) — **PER-AIR SYNC POINT**\n   - Fractional unpack (lines 283-284)\n   - Optional normalization for negative n (lines 285-289)\n   - Transpose evaluation layout (lines 291-300)\n   - TWO iDFTs: `UnivariatePoly::from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft()` x2 (lines 301-310) — **CPU iDFT #2 & #3**\n\n### **Fixed Costs Per AIR**\n\n1. **GPU work**:\n   - 2 kernel launches (zerocheck + logup)\n   - 2 D2H copies with implicit stream synchronization\n   - 1 GPU malloc for main_parts array upload\n\n2. **CPU work** (CPU thread pool):\n   - Constraint extraction from pk\n   - 3 iDFT operations (each O(domain_size * log(domain_size)))\n   - Transpose loops (3x: zerocheck, logup_numer, logup_denom)\n   - Polynomial coefficient construction\n\n### **Batched Descriptor Approach (REVERTED)** \n\n**Commit history**:\n- `0c699f47` (Apr 13): Batch Round 0 descriptor arrays infrastructure added\n  - `Round0ZcCtx` / `Round0LogupCtx` per-AIR descriptor structs\n  - `batched_zerocheck_r0_coset_parallel_kernel` & `batched_logup_r0_coset_parallel_kernel`\n  - Single 1D grid, blocks indexed via `BlockCtx` to find AIR and (coset, x_block)\n  - Infrastructure-only, not wired into pipeline\n\n- `b617e156` (Apr 13, 1 hour later): **REVERTED** with no explanation in commit message\n  - Removed ~959 lines of CUDA kernel and Rust FFI code\n  - Indicates integration or correctness issue discovered during testing\n\n**Why it likely failed**:\n1. **Heterogeneous per-AIR costs**: Batched kernels assume uniform block structure; varying AIR constraint degrees & heights break load balance\n2. **Descriptor overhead**: Per-AIR descriptor structs require additional GPU uploads and kernel parameter passing\n3. **Synchronization complexity**: Mixing per-AIR boundaries in a single kernel is error-prone (noted at line 1063-1065 comment about load balance needing calibration)\n4. **Current workaround**: Multi-stream + round-robin on height-sorted list achieves ~3-4x speedup (662ms → 177-243ms) without per-AIR descriptor overhead\n\n### **File Paths**\n\n- **Main Round 0 logic**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` (lines 99, 126-322, 1038-1194)\n- **Round 0 GPU evaluations**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/round0.rs` (lines 27-154)\n- **GKR multi-stream pattern** (similar): `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/gkr_input.rs` (lines 280-354)\n- **Batched descriptor definition**: `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/cuda/logup_zerocheck.rs` (lines 100-107, currently used for *interpolation*, not Round 0)"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93534bb-5de3-4083-9e85-ad533ac466ab","uuid":"d0ebba73-b1f8-44d6-