{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016SBVHkQkrDLgfDXTKW2X5T","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have the complete picture. Let me compile my findings into a comprehensive report.\n\n## INVESTIGATION SUMMARY: MLE Rounds Per-AIR Overhead in GPU Prover\n\nI've traced the complete MLE round code path in the GPU prover and identified where the per-AIR overhead comes from at APC 300 (623 AIR instances) versus APC 0 (99 instances).\n\n### MAIN MLE ROUND LOOP\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n**Lines:** 566-582\n\n```rust\nfor round in 1..=n_max {\n    let sp_round_evals = prover.sumcheck_polys_batch_eval(round, r[round - 1])?;\n    let batch_s = prover.compute_batch_s_poly(sp_round_evals, num_traces, round, &mu_pows);\n    let batch_s_evals = (1..=s_deg).map(...).collect_vec();\n    transcript.observe_ext(eval);\n    let r_round = transcript.sample_ext();\n    r.push(r_round);\n    prover.prev_s_eval = batch_s.eval_at_point(r_round);\n    prover.fold_mle_evals(round, r_round)?;\n}\n```\n\nEach iteration calls:\n1. **`sumcheck_polys_batch_eval()`** - Evaluates constraints and interactions\n2. **`compute_batch_s_poly()`** - CPU-side batching\n3. **`fold_mle_evals()`** - Folds matrices\n\n---\n\n### CALL CHAIN: sumcheck_polys_batch_eval() - THE PER-AIR BOTTLENECK\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n**Lines:** 1322-1708\n\nThis function is where per-AIR overhead accumulates:\n\n#### **PHASE 1: Metadata Collection (Lines 1337-1472)**\n- Iterates over ALL traces with constraints/interactions\n- Splits into:\n  - **Case A** (round > n_lift): Late evaluation traces, use single-point evaluation\n  - **Case B** (round ≤ n_lift): Early evaluation traces, need interpolation\n\n#### **PHASE 2: Batched Interpolation (Lines 1474-1512)**\n- **Single kernel launch** for all Case B traces - **This is already batched**\n- Uses `batched_interpolate_columns_gpu()` - handles all traces in one call\n\n#### **PHASE 3: Build TraceCtx for Each Trace (Lines 1514-1575)**\nFor each Case B trace:\n- **Line 1558:** `main_ptrs_dev = main_ptrs.to_device()?` - **H2D COPY PER TRACE**\n\n```rust\nlet main_ptrs: Vec<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>> = mats[first_main_idx..]\n    .iter()\n    .map(|m| MainMatrixPtrs {\n        data: m.buffer().as_ptr(),\n        air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, m.width()),\n    })\n    .collect_vec();\nlet main_ptrs_dev = main_ptrs.to_device()?;  // <-- PER-TRACE H2D\n\nearly_eval.push(TraceCtx {\n    trace_idx: meta.trace_idx,\n    air_idx: meta.air_idx,\n    num_y: meta.num_y as u32,\n    main_ptrs_dev,\n    ...\n});\n```\n\n#### **PHASE 3b: Late Trace Evaluation (Lines 1579-1619)**\nFor traces where `round == n_lift + 1` (single-point evaluation):\n- **Line 1406:** `main_ptrs_dev = main_ptrs.to_device()?` - **Another H2D COPY PER TRACE**\n\n```rust\nlet main_ptrs: Vec<MainMatrixPtrs<EF>> = mats[first_main_idx..]\n    .iter()\n    .map(|m| MainMatrixPtrs {\n        data: m.buffer().as_ptr(),\n        air_width: air_width_for_mat(need_rot, m.width()),\n    })\n    .collect_vec();\nlet main_ptrs_dev = main_ptrs.to_device()?;  // <-- PER-TRACE H2D\n\nlate_eval.push(TraceCtx {\n    trace_idx,\n    air_idx,\n    num_y: 1,\n    main_ptrs_dev,\n    ...\n});\n```\n\n#### **PHASE 4: Constraint/Interaction Evaluation (Lines 1621-1705)**\nMultiple sub-phases with per-AIR overhead:\n\n**Lines 1623-1635: Logup Batched**\n```rust\nevaluate_logup_batched(\n    &early_eval,\n    self.pk,\n    d_challenges_ptr,\n    sp_deg as u32,\n    self.monomial_num_y_threshold,\n    &self.logup_combinations,\n    &mut logup_out,\n    &mut self.logup_tilde_evals,\n    self.memory_limit_bytes,\n)?\n```\nThis calls:\n- `LogupMonomialBatch::new()` - Lines 607-746 in `batch_mle_monomial.rs`\n  - Creates H2D transfers for block contexts and logup contexts **per batch**\n\n**Lines 1656-1664: Zerocheck DAG (high num_y)**\n```rust\nevaluate_zerocheck_batched(\n    high_dag_traces,\n    self.pk,\n    lambda_pows,\n    sp_deg as u32,\n    &mut zc_out,\n    self.memory_limit_bytes,\n)?\n```\nThis calls:\n- `ZerocheckMleBatchBuilder::new()` - Lines 127-218 in `batch_mle.rs`\n  - Builds `ZerocheckCtx` per trace (line 192)\n  - H2D transfers: `d_block_ctxs`, `d_zc_ctxs`, `air_offsets` **per batch**\n\n**Lines 1668-1688: Zerocheck Monomial Par-Y (high num_y with monomials)**\n```rust\nlet batch = ZerocheckMonomialParYBatch::new(\n    high_mono_traces,\n    self.pk,\n    &lambda_combs,\n    self.sm_count,\n    sp_deg as u32,\n    None,\n)?\n```\nThis calls:\n- `ZerocheckMonomialParYBatch::new()` - Lines 303-423 in `batch_mle_monomial.rs`\n  - Builds `BlockCtx` per trace within batch (lines 352-368)\n  - H2D transfers: `block_ctxs`, `air_ctxs`, `air_offsets`\n\n**Lines 1692-1705: Zerocheck Monomial (low num_y)**\n```rust\nlet batch = ZerocheckMonomialBatch::new(low_mono_traces, self.pk, &lambda_combs)?\n```\n- `ZerocheckMonomialBatch::new()` - Lines 127-217 in `batch_mle_monomial.rs`\n  - H2D transfers: `block_ctxs`, `air_ctxs`, `air_offsets` **per batch**\n\n---\n\n### INITIALIZATION-TIME PER-AIR OVERHEAD\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`\n**Lines:** 836-910\n\nCalled once during `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys()` (after GKR, before MLE rounds):\n\n**Lines 836-843: Lambda Combinations (for zerocheck monomials)**\n```rust\nfor (air_idx, air_pk) in self.pk.per_air.iter().enumerate() {\n    if air_pk.other_data.zerocheck_monomials.is_some() {\n        self.lambda_combinations[air_idx] = Some(\n            compute_lambda_combinations(self.pk, air_idx, lambda_pows_ref)?\n        );\n    }\n}\n```\n- `compute_lambda_combinations()` - Lines 79-100 in `batch_mle_monomial.rs`\n  - Calls GPU kernel `_precompute_lambda_combinations()` **per AIR with monomials**\n  - Creates `DeviceBuffer::<EF>::with_capacity()` - GPU memory allocation **per AIR**\n\n**Lines 893-910: Logup Combinations (for logup monomials)**\n```rust\nfor (trace_idx, (air_idx, _)) in ctx.per_trace.iter().enumerate() {\n    if air_pk.other_data.interaction_monomials.is_some() {\n        self.logup_combinations[trace_idx] = Some(\n            compute_logup_combinations(\n                self.pk, *air_idx, &self.d_beta_pows, ...\n            )?\n        );\n    }\n}\n```\n- `compute_logup_combinations()` - Lines 509-580 in `batch_mle_monomial.rs`\n  - Calls `_precompute_logup_numer_combinations()` **per AIR**\n  - Calls `_precompute_logup_denom_combinations()` **per AIR**\n  - Creates `DeviceBuffer` allocations **per AIR**\n  - CPU-side loop over interactions (lines 569-573)\n\n---\n\n### BATCHED KERNELS (ALREADY IMPLEMENTED)\n\n**File:** `/home/georg/stark-backend/cuda/src/logup_zerocheck/batch_mle.cu`\n\n1. **`zerocheck_batch_mle_kernel`** (Lines 109-204)\n   - Grid: `(num_blocks, num_x)` - multiple AIRs in single launch\n   - Block reduction + final batched reduction (lines 406-408)\n\n2. **`logup_batch_mle_kernel`** (Lines 206-342)\n   - Grid: `(num_blocks, num_x)` - multiple AIRs in single launch\n   - Batched reduction (lines 439-445)\n\n3. **`batched_final_reduce_block_sums`** (Lines 406, 440)\n   - Grid: `(num_airs, num_x)` - One final reduction per AIR\n   - Already batched for all AIRs\n\n---\n\n### SOURCES OF PER-AIR OVERHEAD IN MLE ROUNDS\n\n1. **Main Pointer Array Copying (EVERY ROUND, EVERY CASE A/B TRACE)**\n   - Lines 1406, 1558: `main_ptrs.to_device()`\n   - Copies array of pointers for each trace's main matrices\n   - **Cannot be easily batched** - different AIRs have different matrix counts\n\n2. **Context Structure H2D Transfers (PER BATCH)**\n   - `ZerocheckMleBatchBuilder::new()` (line 206-208): `d_block_ctxs`, `d_zc_ctxs`, `d_offsets`\n   - `LogupMonomialBatch::new()`: Similar context transfers\n   - `ZerocheckMonomialBatch::new()`: Block and air contexts\n   - `ZerocheckMonomialParYBatch::new()`: Block and air contexts\n\n3. **Batch Decision Logic (VARIABLE NUMBER OF BATCHES)**\n   - `evaluate_zerocheck_batched()` (line 414-502): Memory-aware batching\n   - `evaluate_logup_batched()` (line 505-626): Memory-aware batching\n   - Can create multiple sequential batches **per round**\n   - At high APC, more batches needed → more context setups\n\n4. **Per-AIR Monomial Preprocessing (ONCE, NOT IN LOOP)**\n   - Lambda combinations (lines 836-843): 1 kernel per AIR with monomials\n   - Logup combinations (lines 893-910): 1-2 kernels per AIR with interactions\n   - Not in the MLE round loop, but significant at initialization\n\n---\n\n### KERNEL LAUNCHES PER ROUND AT APC 300 vs APC 0\n\n**At APC 0 (99 AIRs):**\n- Fewer batches needed due to memory constraints being less tight\n- Fewer context structure H2D transfers\n- Fewer kernel launches total\n\n**At APC 300 (623 AIRs):**\n- More traces → likely split into MORE BATCHES\n- Each batch requires: `BlockCtx` H2D, context H2D, offset H2D\n- Each late trace (when `round > n_lift`) requires `main_ptrs_dev.to_device()`\n- This is **sequential per-trace overhead** that doesn't parallelize\n\n---\n\n### SEQUENTIAL (UNBATCHED) OPERATIONS\n\n1. **Main pointer array transfers** (line 1406, 1558)\n   - No way to batch across different AIRs\n   - Each trace needs its own H2D\n\n2. **Batch fragmentation** due to memory limits\n   - `find_batch_end()` (lines 60-86 in batch_mle.rs)\n   - May force traces into sequential batches\n\n3. **Late trace evaluation path** (lines 1579-1619)\n   - Only triggered when `round == n_lift + 1`\n   - But still per-trace `main_ptrs_dev.to_device()`\n\n---\n\nThis is the core of the per-AIR overhead: while the **kernel launches** are batched (multiple AIRs per grid), the **CPU-side context building** and **main pointer array copies** remain sequential per-trace operations that don't scale well with 623 AIRs."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93534bb-5de3-4083-9e85-ad533ac466ab","uuid":"1757f264-b01e