{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_012ferqKKMAghrm1XaDUz5Bf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014mEf56TqBrjpXNRy7DwxE8","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-0330-gpu-round0-poly-extraction\n\nMove the per-AIR polynomial extraction in Round 0 (D2H sync + transpose + iDFT + Lagrange interpolation + coefficient adjustment) from CPU to a small CUDA kernel that runs on the same stream immediately after each evaluation kernel. This eliminates all per-AIR `cudaStreamSynchronize` calls in the multi-stream Round 0 loop and the ~40ms of CPU post-processing per thread, replacing them with a negligible GPU-side computation that writes polynomial coefficients directly into a device-side batch array. A single D2H copy of the complete batch array replaces the current 1246 per-AIR pipeline drains.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":123,"cache_read_input_tokens":154872,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":123},"output_tokens":65,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93534bb-5de3-4083-9e85-ad533ac466ab","uuid":"024d3d73-a6d2-4799-89c6-9a478d986591"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014mEf56TqBrjpXNRy7DwxE8","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md has been updated successfully."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f93534bb-5de3-4083-9e85-ad533ac466ab","uuid":"26bff845-bc83-475a-bf01-1112026566fb","timestamp":"2026-04-14T04:22:27.539Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md","content":"# 2026-04-14-0330-gpu-round0-poly-extraction\n\nMove the per-AIR polynomial extraction in Round 0 (D2H sync + transpose + iDFT + Lagrange interpolation + coefficient adjustment) from CPU to a small CUDA kernel that runs on the same stream immediately after each evaluation kernel. This eliminates all per-AIR `cudaStreamSynchronize` calls in the multi-stream Round 0 loop and the ~40ms of CPU post-processing per thread, replacing them with a negligible GPU-side computation that writes polynomial coefficients directly into a device-side batch array. A single D2H copy of the complete batch array replaces the current 1246 per-AIR pipeline drains.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":3,"newStart":1,"newLines":3,"lines":["-# 2026-04-14-0300-precompute-logup-round0-interaction-rules","+# 2026-04-14-0330-gpu-round0-poly-extraction"," ","-Pre-compute the logup Round 0 interaction evaluation DAG, rules, and weight-index mapping at keygen time, eliminating per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()`, `SymbolicDagBuilder` construction, `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()`, rule encoding, and `d_rules` device upload in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. The keygen code already builds this identical DAG (pkey.rs:116-142) but discards everything except `buffer_size`. Keeping the full pre-computed rules and a compact weight mapping table allows the hot path to skip all DAG reconstruction and only compute challenge-dependent weights (~0.2ms per AIR instead of ~1.0ms). At APC 300 with 623 AIRs across 8 round-robin-balanced threads, this eliminates ~0.8ms of CPU overhead per AIR, yielding ~50-80ms wall-time improvement for Round 0.","+Move the per-AIR polynomial extraction in Round 0 (D2H sync + transpose + iDFT + Lagrange interpolation + coefficient adjustment) from CPU to a small CUDA kernel that runs on the same stream immediately after each evaluation kernel. This eliminates all per-AIR `cudaStreamSynchronize` calls in the multi-stream Round 0 loop and the ~40ms of CPU post-processing per thread, replacing them with a negligible GPU-side computation that writes polynomial coefficients directly into a device-side batch array. A single D2H copy of the complete batch array replaces the current 1246 per-AIR pipeline drains."]}],"originalFile":"# 2026-04-14-0300-precompute-logup-round0-interaction-rules\n\nPre-compute the logup Round 0 interaction evaluation DAG, rules, and weight-index mapping at keygen time, eliminating per-AIR `SymbolicConstraints::from()`, `SymbolicDagBuilder` construction, `SymbolicRulesGpu::new()`, rule encoding, and `d_rules` device upload in `evaluate_round0_interactions_gpu`. The keygen code already builds this identical DAG (pkey.rs:116-142) but discards everything except `buffer_size`. Keeping the full pre-computed rules and a compact weight mapping table allows the hot path to skip all DAG reconstruction and only compute challenge-dependent weights (~0.2ms per AIR instead of ~1.0ms). At APC 300 with 623 AIRs across 8 round-robin-balanced threads, this eliminates ~0.8ms of CPU overhead per AIR, yielding ~50-80ms wall-time improvement for Round 0.\n"}}
