{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0121LgyHrpTNAhrSFftqYqYz","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 2026-04-14-0330-gpu-round0-poly-extraction\n2\t\n3\tMove the per-AIR polynomial extraction in Round 0 (D2H sync + transpose + iDFT + Lagrange interpolation + coefficient adjustment) from CPU to a small CUDA kernel that runs on the same stream immediately after each evaluation kernel. This eliminates all per-AIR `cudaStreamSynchronize` calls in the multi-stream Round 0 loop and the ~40ms of CPU post-processing per thread, replacing them with a negligible GPU-side computation that writes polynomial coefficients directly into a device-side batch array. A single D2H copy of the complete batch array replaces the current 1246 per-AIR pipeline drains.\n4\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01GNRJrb1ZmSyjfXvXwDQXiJ","session_id":"f93534bb-5de3-4083-9e85-ad533ac466ab","uuid":"ddf965ba-9966-438d-be79-2ce847b18a11","timestamp":"2026-04-14T04:24:30.667Z"}
