{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019J3NwNoNw2nn8DpXey87cL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q1KfgaZz2xthmPrenpaYXs","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Review plan iteration 2","prompt":"You are reviewing an updated optimization plan for a GPU prover system. This is the second review iteration. The first review found these issues:\n1. DFT variant was contradictory (Cooley-Tukey vs Bowers) — FIXED: now explicitly says Bowers\n2. Output coefficient layout not specified — FIXED: now specifies interleaved layout matching poly.rs:678\n3. \"Trimming trailing zeros\" for polynomial reconstruction — FIXED: now uses per-AIR known lengths\n4. None vs zero-polynomial semantics — FIXED: now explicitly reconstructs empty polynomials for absent AIRs\n5. DeviceBuffer sharing across threads — FIXED: now specifies raw pointer passing via usize cast\n6. Performance estimate was optimistic — FIXED: reduced from 70ms to 50ms savings\n\nRead these files and verify the fixes:\n1. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/review_guideline.md` — the review standard\n2. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt/context.md` — project context\n3. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/task.md` — the task\n4. `/home/georg/stark-backend/autoopt-results/2026-04-14-0330-gpu-round0-poly-extraction/plan.md` — the UPDATED plan\n\nAlso read these source files to verify claims:\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs` lines 118-322 (process_air_round0)\n- `/home/georg/stark-backend/crates/stark-backend/src/prover/poly.rs` lines 621-683 (from_geometric_cosets_evals_idft)\n\nReview this plan following the review guideline. Return your response in the format: Findings, Improvements, Assessment.\n\nFocus on:\n- Are the previous findings properly addressed?\n- Any remaining design-level blockers?\n- Is the plan specific enough to implement without guessing?\n- Is the performance estimate supported