{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YDa4tok8fXsrBvvrRmM954","type":"tool_result","content":"142\t### Change 4: Pre-allocate device batch polynomial array\n143\t\n144\t**File**: `crates/cuda-backend/src/logup_zerocheck/mod.rs`, inside `sumcheck_uni_round0_polys`\n145\t\n146\tAfter work item construction (around line 1036):\n147\t1. Compute per-AIR polynomial lengths:\n148\t   - For each `trace_idx`, record `poly_len_zc = (d-1) * skip_domain` if AIR has constraints, else 0.\n149\t   - `poly_len_logup = d * skip_domain` if AIR has interactions, else 0.\n150\t   - Store these in a `Vec<(usize, usize, usize)>` (one per trace_idx: `(zc_len, numer_len, denom_len)`).\n151\t2. Compute `max_poly_len`: maximum of all lengths. With `d_max=4`, `l_skip=4`: `max(3*16, 4*16) = 64`.\n152\t3. Allocate `DeviceBuffer<EF>::with_capacity(3 * num_present_airs * max_poly_len)`.\n153\t4. `fill_zero` the buffer (zero coefficients = zero polynomial, functionally equivalent to empty).\n154\t5. Compute the per-trace offset mapping as `usize` values:\n155\t   - `zc_offset[trace_idx] = (2 * num_present_airs + trace_idx) * max_poly_len`\n156\t   - `numer_offset[trace_idx] = (2 * trace_idx) * max_poly_len`\n157\t   - `denom_offset[trace_idx] = (2 * trace_idx + 1) * max_poly_len`\n158\t6. Pass offset mapping and raw device pointer to worker threads.\n159\t\n160\tMemory: `3 * 623 * 64 * 16 = ~1.9MB`. Negligible.\n161\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q1KfgaZz2xthmPrenpaYXs","session_id":"f93534bb-5de3-4083-9e85-ad533ac466ab","uuid":"ceecfe87-5e14-42b4-a334-d4ac30dcaeab","timestamp":"2026-04-14T04:31:42.324Z"}
